"Movement-caused disease describes disorders traditionally understood as arising from a disturbance in the meridian's own qi flow — its movement — producing symptoms that tend to appear suddenly along the meridian's actual pathway, such as pain that follows the meridian's course closely. Generated disease describes a broader category: disorders the meridian is associated with through the organ or tissue it connects to, which can include symptoms with no obvious direct connection to the meridian's physical pathway at all, tracing back to the meridian by association with its organ rather than by direct route.": "0392d751f570",
